      "steps": [
        "Step 1 (Provisioning): Provision Amazon Data Firehose inside your private VPC subnets with appropriate Multi-AZ redundancy.",
        "Step 2 (IAM Permissions): Attach an IAM execution role granting least-privilege permissions to required S3 buckets and KMS keys.",
        "Step 3 (Pipeline Integration): Connect Amazon Data Firehose to upstream data streams, feature stores, or downstream inference endpoints.",
        "Step 4 (Observability): Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms on key operational metrics and enable AWS CloudTrail API logging.",
        "Step 5 (Cost & Scale): Implement Auto-Scaling policies or lifecycle transition rules to optimize ongoing cloud spend."
      ],
      "mechanics": "Amazon Data Firehose communicates with other AWS services via encrypted HTTPS REST APIs signed with AWS Signature Version 4 (SigV4). Data at rest is secured using AWS KMS Customer Managed Keys (CMKs) with envelope encryption. Network traffic remains entirely within the AWS internal backbone when accessed via VPC Endpoints (AWS PrivateLink)."
